Can't the original poster just download the binary nethack-343-linux-X11.tgz
(from here: http://www.nethack.org/v343/ports/download-linux.html ) and
install that, no compiling needed.

Alternatively you could just download one of the rpms and convert it to a
deb (Linspire is debain based so that should work) with the command:
alien -d _RPM_FILE_
then you can just install the mew deb with the command:
dpkg -i _DEB_FILE_

At least that's how I'd do it in Ubuntu if nethack wasn't easily available
in the repositories. 

Thinking about it, if you want to learn about Linux then learning how to
compile software is a very important early step, so it is worth learning to
do things the hard way. 

